								<p>During my internship, I learned that clean code is more than keeping a project organized. It makes code easier to read, debug, update, and understand. I practiced using clear names, consistent formatting, and proper file structures. These habits helped me work with unfamiliar code, fix issues faster, and collaborate better with other developers.</p>
