								<h3 class="h3-sub">How We Built Servease From Our First Capstone Idea</h3>
								<p>We started by planning the purpose, users, and main features of Servease. After defining the system flow, we created the UI/UX mockups and reviewed them as a team. Once we agreed on the design, we built the static frontend, connected Laravel with SQL, added the backend logic and CMS, then tested each feature before deployment.</p>
								<h3 class="h3-sub">A Service Booking Platform With Four User Roles</h3>
								<p>Servease has four main roles. Customers search for services and create bookings. Providers manage their services and booking requests. System admins handle daily platform activities. Super admins manage users, system settings, and higher-level access. Each role has specific features based on its responsibilities.</p>
								<h3 class="h3-sub">Brevo Helped Us Add Email Verification to Our Capstone System</h3>
								<p>We used Brevo’s free SMTP service to handle email verification and authentication emails. The free plan provides up to 300 emails per day, which suited our capstone needs. We connected it to Servease so users could receive verification emails during account registration and authentication.</p>
